KMA 1.5.1: print 64-bit counters with <inttypes.h> formats

Several fprintf calls pass uint64_t values with %lu/%ld. That is only
correct where `long` is 64-bit (LP64). On ILP32 targets such as wasm32
(the openpathogen fallback engine for browsers without Memory64), the
varargs are misread and every later field is garbage: .mapstat columns
shift (readCount, bpTotal, depth ... all wrong) and progress lines and the
QC JSON print nonsense. .res is unaffected (it uses its own formats).

Use PRIu64 for uint64_t arguments (and PRId64 with a cast for time_t in
the XML header). On LP64 native and wasm64 builds the output is unchanged;
clang -Wformat is now clean on native, wasm64 and wasm32.

